Falsifies `intrusive_queue::verification::a_popped_node_leaves_with_a_clear_link`.

The defect: `pop_front` stops clearing the popped node's link. The line reads as housekeeping,
because the queue never follows that link again once the node has left, and the queue's own order
stays right. A popped node then carries a pointer into the queue it left, and a later reader of
the node follows it.

Expected to fail: the harness's assertion that a popped node's `next` is `None`, whenever two or
more nodes were queued.

diff --git a/crates/intrusive_queue/src/lib.rs b/crates/intrusive_queue/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/intrusive_queue/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/intrusive_queue/src/lib.rs
@@ -296,7 +296,6 @@
             if self.head.is_none() {
                 self.tail = None;
             }
-            (*node.as_ptr()).set_next(None);
         }
         // Wrapping: `head` was `Some`, so `len >= 1`. The Kani proof below holds `len` to the
         // model's count after every step, so a wrapped decrement would fail it.
